    "title": "Our mission",
    "minutes": 15,
    "summary": "The statement, our focus, and the four-question check before anything goes out.",
    "html": "<blockquote class=\"mission\">We are a volunteer effort by Apopka seniors. We read the public record, we tell people what it actually says, and we correct false claims with documents anyone can look up themselves. We operate independently, without compensation, and without connection to any campaign, party, or candidate.</blockquote>\n<h2>Our Focus</h2>\n<p>Our focus is misinformation about the City of Apopka&rsquo;s government and its personnel — its commissioners, its staff, and its projects.</p>\n<p>There are people in this community who are constantly disruptive, who attack commissioners and City projects with claims that are not accurate, and who have had the floor to themselves because nobody was standing next to those claims with the documents. That is what we are here to change.</p>\n<p><b>We are the voice of reason and information.</b> When a commissioner, a staff member, or a City project is hit with a false claim, we find the record that settles it and we get the truth out.</p>\n<p>We are not any one commissioner&rsquo;s group. The trigger for our work is the false claim, not who it was aimed at.</p>\n<h2>Why This Wording Matters</h2>\n<p>Every phrase in the mission statement is a commitment we can be held to:</p>\n<ul><li><b>&ldquo;We read the public record&rdquo;</b> — Our authority comes from documents.</li><li><b>&ldquo;What it actually says&rdquo;</b> — Including when the record is incomplete or ambiguous. We report what is there.</li><li><b>&ldquo;Documents anyone can look up themselves&rdquo;</b> — Every factual claim we make is independently verifiable by the person hearing it. We are not asking anyone to take our word for it.</li><li><b>&ldquo;Independently, without compensation&rdquo;</b> — Nobody pays us and nobody directs us.</li></ul>\n<h2>The Mission Check</h2>\n<p>Before any material is distributed, four questions must be answered &ldquo;yes&rdquo;:</p>\n<ol><li>Is every factual claim traceable to a primary source document?</li><li>Is the source identified specifically enough that a stranger could retrieve it?</li><li>Have two people verified it independently?</li><li>Would we publish this same document if it cut the other way?</li></ol>\n<p>If any answer is &ldquo;no,&rdquo; it does not go out. Any volunteer may call a mission check at any meeting, and the Record Director must answer it.</p>\n<h2>Mission Drift Prevention</h2>\n<ul><li>The Record Director maintains the Verification Log — every published claim, its source, its two verifiers, and the date.</li><li>The Overall Coordinator reviews all materials monthly against the four questions.</li><li>The Verification Log is available to any volunteer who asks to see it.</li></ul>"
