    "summary": "Nothing goes public until the documents are in hand. The four findings and only four.",
    "html": "<p>Nothing goes out as fact until the documents are in hand. This phase is the reason the group can be trusted later.</p>\n<h2>Step 1 — Identify the Claims in Circulation</h2>\n<p><i>Record Director, with all teams:</i></p>\n<ol><li>Collect from volunteers every specific claim they have personally heard about the City, its commissioners, its staff, or its projects, in the words they heard it</li><li>Write each one down verbatim — do not paraphrase into something more reasonable</li><li>Group duplicates</li><li>Rank by how often each is heard</li></ol>\n<p>The claim as it actually circulates is the one that needs answering. A cleaned-up version answers nothing.</p>\n<h2>Step 2 — Pull the Documents</h2>\n<p>For each ranked claim:</p>\n<ol><li>Identify which public record would confirm or refute it</li><li>Retrieve it — agency website, clerk&rsquo;s office, or Chapter 119 public records request</li><li>Log the request date if it is outstanding</li><li>Read the whole document, not the part that helps</li></ol>\n<h2>Step 3 — Write the Finding</h2>\n<p>For each claim, one of four findings — and only these four:</p>\n<div class=\"tscroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Finding</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Supported</b></td><td>The record confirms the claim. We say so.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Contradicted</b></td><td>The record shows something different. We show what.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Partially accurate</b></td><td>Part is right, part is not. We separate them.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Not established</b></td><td>The record does not address it, or is not yet available. We say that and say what we&rsquo;ve requested.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2>Step 4 — Two-Person Verification</h2>\n<p>Every finding is independently verified per the Two-Person Rule before it enters any material. Log it.</p>\n<h2>Step 5 — Build the Materials</h2>\n<p><b>The Fact Sheet</b> (one page, front and back if needed)</p>\n<ul><li>Header: group name, &ldquo;What the Record Shows,&rdquo; and the date</li><li>Each entry: the claim as circulated → the finding → the citation</li><li>Footer: mission statement, how to reach us, and how to look these up independently</li></ul>\n<p><b>The Claim Response Card</b> (wallet size, for volunteers)</p>\n<ul><li>Claim → finding → citation → a plain sentence to say</li></ul>\n<p><b>The Source Binder</b> (one per team)</p>\n<ul><li>Printed copies of every cited document, tabbed and indexed</li><li>The Educator carries it to presentations. Handing someone the actual page ends most arguments in a way no summary can.</li></ul>"
