    "title": "Success metrics",
    "minutes": 10,
    "summary": "What we measure, who owns each number, and how often.",
    "html": "<div class=\"tscroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Owner</th><th>Cadence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Conversations by channel</td><td>Data Manager</td><td>Weekly</td></tr><tr><td>Distinct claims logged</td><td>Data Manager</td><td>Weekly</td></tr><tr><td>Claims with a verified finding published</td><td>Record Director</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Median time from new claim to published finding</td><td>Record Director</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Unanswered questions resolved into documents</td><td>Record Director</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Presentations delivered and organizations reached</td><td>Data Manager</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Public comments delivered at meetings</td><td>Data Manager</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Materials distributed</td><td>Resource Coordinator</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Requests for updates (opt-ins)</td><td>Data Manager</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Corrections we issued on our own work</td><td>Record Director</td><td>Monthly</td></tr><tr><td>Volunteer retention</td><td>Overall Coordinator</td><td>Monthly</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><b>Median time from claim to published finding is the number that matters most.</b> It is the measure of whether we are actually answering misinformation or just documenting it after the fact.</p>\n<p><b>The correction count is a health indicator, not a failure count.</b> A group that never corrects itself is either not checking or not admitting.</p>"
