    "summary": "Not written yet. The template and what has to go in it.",
    "html": "<div class=\"hold\"><div class=\"t\">This content does not exist yet</div><p>The Fact Sheet holds the group&rsquo;s actual findings on actual claims. It is written by the Record Director in Phase 2, and no entry goes in until it has cleared two-person verification. Nobody should carry a blank version anywhere.</p></div>\n<pre>APOPKA SENIORS FOR GOOD GOVERNANCE\nWhat the Record Shows — Version ___ — [Date]\n\nWe are volunteers. We read public records and tell you what they say.\nDon't take our word for anything below — every citation tells you\nexactly where to look it up yourself.\n\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\nWHAT'S BEING SAID: \"[claim, in the words it circulates]\"\n\nWHAT THE RECORD SHOWS: [Supported / Contradicted /\nPartially accurate / Not established]\n\n[One to three sentences describing what the document says.]\n\nWHERE TO FIND IT: [Agency], [document type], [date],\n[item/page]. Available at [location or URL], or by request\nat [office].\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[Repeat per claim]\n\nSTILL OPEN: [Claims where we have requested records but\nhave not received them. Date requested: ______]\n\nIF WE GET SOMETHING WRONG, we publish a correction within\n72 hours through every channel the original went out through.\nTell us: [contact]\n\nOUR MISSION: We are a volunteer effort by Apopka seniors. We read the\npublic record, we tell people what it actually says, and we correct\nfalse claims with documents anyone can look up themselves. We operate\nindependently, without compensation, and without connection to any\ncampaign, party, or candidate.\n\nCONTACT: [Name], [Phone], [Email]</pre>",
